the 60s era Mondo films that that this movie

00:00:54.570 --> 00:01:00.930
is sort of an homage to and sort of what you
see is interesting about the genre?

00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:09.409
Speaker 6: Well, I think if I if I have my
genres right, it's nouvelle vague.

00:01:09.409 --> 00:01:13.780
It's Godard and Chabrol and Varda and Truffaut.

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:16.040
The new wave they called it.

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:23.110
I think of this film sort of as the boot to
surf, which is Godard's film only in color.

00:01:23.110 --> 00:01:30.040
There were there are stories that Godard actually
knew that what he was doing was bad, but that

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:32.500
was the whole point.

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:39.500
So he was trying to look at the language of
film and develop a new syntax, a new way of

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:44.900
making films sort of the way Bertolt Brecht
does with what it's called very Freemans effect,

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:49.409
which is to distance an audience to keep them
aware that it is filmic, that it is a film

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:52.290
that is a fiction, it is a narrative.

00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:57.689
It relates to something that is up for the
audience to create for themselves

00:01:57.689 --> 00:02:03.060
