you agree that this type of analysis of film

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:17.200
has become sorely lacking sort of in popular
culture in the United States at this point

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:18.970
in time.

00:02:18.970 --> 00:02:19.970
Do you agree with that?

00:02:19.970 --> 00:02:27.360
I mean, it seems to me that the richness of
the discussion of film in this style is not

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:29.880
what it once was in popular society.

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:32.500
Speaker 6: Certainly in America.

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:36.400
Cut in America film is considered a product.

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:40.500
A studio has a certain studio works, is owned
by a corporation.

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:46.570
That corporation has obligations to its shareholders
to produce the profit they produce.

00:02:46.570 --> 00:02:49.500
This thing called a film cinema.

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:54.980
They show the cinema and they try to reach
as broad an audience as possible, so they

00:02:54.980 --> 00:03:00.260
either play down to that audience or through
the media that they also control.

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:04.269
They create reviews that make the thing seem
as vacuous as possible.

00:03:04.269 --> 00:03:08.660
So it's not send anybody before they they're
sitting in the seats watching it.

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:09.830
